<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton output reaches 49,648 bales.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton output reaches 49,648 bales.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pakistan Cotton Ginners Association said on Wednesday new crop cotton output had reached a provisional 49,648 375-lb bales in the first month of 1997/98 (July-June), all of it from Sindh province.</p>
<p>Arrivals of raw cotton from Punjab province, Pakistan's main cotton growing region, begin at the end of August or early September.</p>
<p>The Association gave no comparative figures from last year.</p>
<p>-- Karachi Newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
